content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "User",
      "description": "Person participating in discussions and interactions",
      "attributes": [
        "History"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "History",
      "description": "Record of a User’s past activity"
    },
    {
      "name": "Discussion Thread",
      "description": "Main conversation container in the forum",
      "attributes": [
        "Topic",
        "Post",
        "Flag"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Topic",
      "description": "Subject that a Discussion Thread focuses on"
    },
    {
      "name": "Post",
      "description": "Message contributed to a Discussion Thread",
      "attributes": [
        "Reply",
        "Vote"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Reply",
      "description": "Response to a Post"
    },
    {
      "name": "Vote",
      "description": "User feedback expressing support for a Post"
    },
    {
      "name": "Flag",
      "description": "Marker indicating that content needs Moderator attention"
    },
    {
      "name": "Moderator",
      "description": "User responsible for keeping discussions safe and organized"
    },
    {
      "name": "Forum Guidelines",
      "description": "Rules that define acceptable content"
    },
    {
      "name": "Content Reviewer",
      "description": "User who highlights valuable content and creates summaries"
    },
    {
      "name": "Highlight",
      "description": "Mark indicating a notable Discussion Thread"
    },
    {
      "name": "FAQ",
      "description": "Collection of common questions and useful answers"
    },
    {
      "name": "Bookmark",
      "description": "Saved link to a Discussion Thread for later access"
    },
    {
      "name": "Category",
      "description": "Grouping used to organize related Discussion Threads",
      "attributes": [
        "Topic",
        "Discussion Thread"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Lock",
      "description": "State preventing new Posts in a Discussion Thread"
    },
    {
      "name": "System",
      "description": "Automated process handling recommendations and notifications"
    },
    {
      "name": "Recommendation",
      "description": "Suggested Discussion Threads for a User",
      "attributes": [
        "Discussion Thread"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Notification",
      "description": "Message informing a User about activity related to them"
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Moderation": {
      "objects": [
        "Moderator",
        "Forum Guidelines",
        "Category",
        "Topic",
        "Lock",
        "Flag",
        "Discussion Thread"
      ]
    },
    "System Functions": {
      "objects": [
        "System",
        "History",
        "Recommendation",
        "Discussion Thread"
      ]
    },
    "Discussion": {
      "objects": [
        "User",
        "History",
        "Discussion Thread",
        "Topic",
        "Post",
        "Vote",
        "Reply",
        "Bookmark"
      ]
    },
    "Highlights": {
      "objects": [
        "Content Reviewer",
        "Highlight",
        "FAQ"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- In case an object appears in multiple bounded contexts, suggest a name change.
- Also suggest a name change if the meaning of the object is too similar to an object from another bounded context
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "Moderation": {
      "derived from": "Moderation Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Moderator",
        "Forum Guidelines",
        "Category",
        "Category Topic",
        "Lock",
        "Flag",
        "Discussion Entry"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Topic -> Category Topic",
        "Discussion Thread -> Discussion Entry"
      ]
    },
    "System Functions": {
      "derived from": "System Functions Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "System",
        "History Data",
        "Recommendation",
        "Recommended Discussion"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "History -> History Data",
        "Discussion Thread -> Recommended Discussion"
      ]
    },
    "Discussion": {
      "derived from": "Discussion Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "User",
        "Personal History",
        "Discussion Thread",
        "Discussion Topic",
        "Post",
        "Vote",
        "Reply",
        "Bookmark"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "History -> Personal History",
        "Topic -> Discussion Topic"
      ]
    },
    "Highlights": {
      "derived from": "Highlights Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Content Reviewer",
        "Highlight",
        "FAQ"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    }
  }
}
```
